# t1-notify-fix -> lead (core)

Nothing in a hot file is needed: no protocol method, no module line, no Cargo edge, no SERVICE_PENDING change.

What the lead should know when compiling:
- `mixdog-connections/src/notifier.rs` now holds the one final-answer watcher (`AnswerWatch`, `TurnTracker`, `TurnFacts`, `TurnEnd`, `WatchWake`, `Settled`, `StepReport`)
  used by `ServerNotifier` and by `mixdog-app-server-daemon` `domain_seams/notify_producer.rs`; the timing constants (`STABILIZE_MS`, `LEAD_FINISHED_MS`, `ANSWER_POLL_MS`,
  `READ_RETRY_MAX_MS`, `READ_FAILURE_LIMIT`, `READ_DEADLINE`) are `pub` there and no longer defined twice. New test file `notifier_watch_tests.rs` (mod line in notifier.rs).
- `mixdog-connections/src/server_feed.rs`: `FinalAnswer::parse` is `pub` (notify_sources.rs's copy of it is deleted).
- `mixdog-core-domains/src/notify`: `SkipReason::diagnostic()`, `NotificationEngine::toast_refusal()` (why this PC shows no toast), a preview test.
- The producer's phone wait pushes are one per session that shows the approval (under that session), as push-notifier.ts sent them; this PC's toast stays once per approval.
- The producer writes `[mixdog-turn-notification] turn-notification-<step> {json}` lines to the daemon log for the steps the core owns (detected, suppressed with its
  reason, waiting-answer, read-failed, cancelled); the host writes the steps it owns (requested, os-show, sound, closed, failed, clicked) to the desktop diagnostics
  (apps/desktop/pending-wire/t1-notify-fix.wire).
- Applied fragments removed: g99-notify-producer.kept (both trees), nl-notify-2.wire, nl-notify-2-followup.wire.
- Still to run by the lead (not done here, cargo is not run): the producer, watcher and notifier tests, and a composed toast / phone-push smoke.
